{{/*
family: web-ui
what: flow
transports: netflow9, ipfix
reference: RFC 3954 (NetFlow v9), RFC 7011 (IPFIX)
verification: reference
*/}}
{{define "does"}}The values to enter in the device's flow export page so it sends flow records to Woodshed as {{if eq .Transport "ipfix"}}IPFIX{{else}}NetFlow v9{{end}}.{{end}}

{{define "parts"}}
@@part steps - In the device's web page, open its flow export (NetFlow or IPFIX) settings and enter
Flow export: on
Collector address: {{.Address}}
Port: {{.Port}} (UDP)
Version: {{if eq .Transport "ipfix"}}IPFIX (sometimes listed as NetFlow v10){{else}}NetFlow v9{{end}}
Interfaces: the ones whose traffic you want to see
Active timeout: 60 seconds (how often long flows are reported)
Template refresh: 60 seconds, if asked
{{end}}

{{define "notes"}}
Field names differ between devices; some call the collector a target or a server.
If the page offers sampling, note the rate: Woodshed shows counts as exported and scaled by it.
{{end}}

{{define "check"}}Woodshed's Flows view lists the device as an exporter within a minute or two.{{end}}
